invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: a QUIC host object stops packaging the table, quic_aes_soft.c,
  beside the AES instructions, so aes.c calls aes_soft_expand_round_keys
  and aes_soft_cipher_block for the public keys of a session whose caller
  did not set CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, and no source in the object
  defines them. A linker would refuse the image, but it names a missing
  symbol, not the object that lost its source. The lint's host QUIC rows
  require the table beside the instructions.

--- old
             $(if $(filter quic-nonblocking,$(TRANSPORT)),quic_aes_soft.c),$(AES_IMPL)))
--- new
             ,$(AES_IMPL)))
